      "writtenOn": "2023-12-27T20:56:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a little confused what this is being used for since it looks like all we do with this set is add/insert addresses via track/untrack. Also, with that - why do we need track/untrack commands?",
      "revId": "00502d20643277e1362035b1169ef25b84ea5f55",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7be94d37_35d42827",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/client/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1963520
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T00:14:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When btclient registers itself for updates from the BatteryService, we receive all battery updates for all connected devices. If, say, we only wanted to monitor the battery updates for a single device, this could result in excess information. The track/untrack commands allow us to filter for only the battery updates for addresses we are interested in, which are stored in this address filter.",
      "parentUuid": "d4bef380_27c7ce08",
      "revId": "00502d20643277e1362035b1169ef25b84ea5f55",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
